==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|it|la|[[ad]] [[paene]]||almost}}. Unrelated to {{m|it|pena||pain, punishment}}.

Compare Catalan {{m|ca|a penes}}, Esperanto {{m|eo|apenaŭ}}, French {{m|fr|à peine}}, Ido {{m|io|apene}}, Portuguese {{m|pt|apenas}}, and Spanish {{m|es|apenas}}.

===Adverb===
{{it-adv}}

# [[barely]], [[hardly]]
# (''in regards to time'') [[just]]; moments ago, [[recently]]
# [[as soon as]]
#: ''Vi risponderemo '''appena''' possibile.'' = “We will reply to you as soon as possible.”

Note that ''non appena'' has the same meaning as ''appena''.

